# Allowlist, not a blocklist. The repo is ~1 GB (video-studio 627M, output 168M,
# screenshots 145M) and the two Dockerfiles between them COPY five small files.
# Without this, every `gcloud builds submit` uploaded the whole gigabyte to build
# a ~200 MB image, on every deploy.
#
# Blocklisting was the wrong shape here: a new generated-asset folder would
# silently rejoin the context. Ignore everything, then re-admit exactly what is
# COPYed. IF YOU ADD A `COPY` TO EITHER DOCKERFILE, ADD IT HERE TOO -- the build
# will fail with "file not found" pointing straight back at this file.

*

# ./Dockerfile -- the pipeline image
!requirements.txt
!startup.sh

# ./cloud/Dockerfile -- 24/7 Bez on Cloud Run
!scripts/bez_agent.py
!scripts/bez_socket.py
!cloud/entrypoint.sh
